    "updated_at": "2021-03-15T19:06:34Z",
    "body": "This seems somewhat reasonable, but I suspect it'd be better to approach this holistically as part of making all the [app manifest](https://w3c.github.io/manifest/) properties (such as screenshots, background color, splash screen, etc.) color-scheme aware. So I suspect this would best be tackled by opening an issue at https://github.com/w3c/manifest/. Then `<meta name=\"theme-color\">` can continue to only be used for simple cases.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, please note https://whatwg.org/faq#adding-new-features : it's best to start with a use case, not a solution. In this case your use case appears to be dark mode vs. light mode, so that points toward something less general than the full power of media queries.",
