    "updated_at": "2021-03-15T22:18:19Z",
    "body": "Also, unless I'm misreading [this](https://w3c.github.io/manifest/#theme_color-member)\r\n> [...] a document may override the [default theme color](https://w3c.github.io/manifest/#dfn-default-theme-color) through the inclusion of a valid [[HTML](https://w3c.github.io/manifest/#bib-html)] [meta\r\n(https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-meta-element) element whose [name](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-meta-name) attribute value is `\"theme-color\"`.\r\n\r\nthat seems to suggest that the `<meta name=\"theme-color\">` in HTML takes precedence over anything specified in the manifest.\r\n\r\nI'd also like to avoid having situations where network latency causes there to be a color change flash (see the example I describe in the issue description above).",
