    "created_at": "2021-03-15T22:56:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-15T22:56:46Z",
    "body": "I think one of the big questions at hand is — are `media` queries as an HTML attribute the right solution? Or would a different keyword / different attribute on the `<meta>` tag be better? It seems more complex to use `media`, because media queries do a lot of things. But also, `media` is more in line with the rest of HTML — not something weirdly bespoke / different syntax or concepts than what works in elsewhere CSS. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
