    "updated_at": "2021-06-15T09:31:23Z",
    "body": "That wouldn't solve either of the use cases I mentioned. Sorry if I wasn't clear: I wasn't talking about a site having two stylesheets, one for dark and one for light. I was talking about a site having many, many stylesheets (in a Zen Garden kind of way). On [my site](https://adactio.com), for example, I have multiple style sheets for different theming and each one might have it's own media queries for dark and light mode.\r\n\r\nAnd for the situation where the theme colour changes to match the contents of the page, JavaScript is currently the only way to do it (that's unrelated to dark and light modes though).",
